WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
Midnight on the battlements.

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.810
A figure in armour
appears, glowing faintly.

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.580
A young man from Wittenberg,
Luther's university,

4
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.750
calls out to it: "Be thou a spirit
of health or goblin damn’d".

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.900
It beckons.

6
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.440
He steps towards it.

7
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.380
His friends hold him back.

8
00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.210
Angel?

9
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.110
Devil?

10
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.030
Or a soul in purgatory?

11
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.940
So should he trust it?

12
00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.750
In this mission, you'll see why a
ghost from purgatory was a problem,

13
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.840
in a Church of England that
had rejected purgatory.

14
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.590
You'll hear the Ghost
describe its own prison-house,

15
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.710
and Hamlet fear that
it "May be the devil".

16
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.670
And you'll follow him to
the graveyard in Act 5,

17
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.550
and Yorick's skull.

18
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.680
Your mission: decide
whether he should trust it.
